mpv: embed the macOS video output (gpu-context=macvk) in a host NSView

With --wid set to the address of an NSView, MacCommon adds mpv's view as an
autoresizing subview of that host view instead of creating a window. It
follows the view's frame and the host window's backing-properties and screen
changes. The view's pixel size and screen are cached on the main thread for
the VO thread, so resizing never waits on the main thread, and the display
link, ICC profile, display name and HiDPI scale follow the host window's
screen. An embedded view draws while its window is visible, and always the
first frame, as mpv's own window does.

One change outside --wid: context_mac.m's resize now returns false when the
drawable is under 1 px in either dimension, where it used to call
ra_vk_ctx_resize(0, 0) for a zero-sized window.

